Q: SwiftUI force device rotation programmatically A: <p>For some reason other solutions including few similar but without a call to <code>setNeedsUpdateOfSupportedInterfaceOrientations</code> that used requestGeometryUpdate and few other methods did not work for me. Here is a solution that worked for me:</p>
<pre><code>@main
struct MyApp: App {
    @UIApplicationDelegateAdaptor private var appDelegate: AppDelegate

    var body: some Scene {
        WindowGroup {
            ContentView()
        }
    }
}

final class AppDelegate: NSObject, UIApplicationDelegate {
    static var supportedOrientation: UIInterfaceOrientationMask = .all {
        didSet {
            UIApplication.shared.connectedScenes.forEach { scene in
                (scene as? UIWindowScene)?.windows.forEach { window in
                    window.rootViewController?.setNeedsUpdateOfSupportedInterfaceOrientations()
                }
            }
        }
    }

    func application(_ application: UIApplication, supportedInterfaceOrientationsFor window: UIWindow?) -&gt; UIInterfaceOrientationMask {
        return Self.supportedOrientation
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>Then just set <code>AppDelegate.supportedOrientation = .landscapeRight</code> when you open the view you want to always open in landscape and when you close it you call <code>AppDelegate.supportedOrientation = .all</code> and it should work.</p>

Q: How to align text/span inside div to the right? A: <p>Wrap both the characters and the remaining paragraph tags in a div container, and give it <code>display: flex;</code> and <code>justify-content: space-between;</code></p>
<pre><code></code></pre>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>.stats {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;
  align-content: center;
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;div&gt;
  &lt;textarea id="input" placeholder="Type some text here..." maxlength="423"&gt;&lt;/textarea&gt;

  &lt;div class="stats"&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Characters: &lt;span id="characters"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p class="right"&gt;Remaining: &lt;span id="remaining"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;</code></pre>
